hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"56","\The apparel dearest to Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) was the shirt.”"""
"57","\The apparel dearest to Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) was the shirt he used to wear.”"""
"58","“The sleeve of the shirt of Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) extended to the wrist.”"
"59","“I came to Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) in a group of fewer than ten men from the Muzaina tribe, so that we might pay homage to him, and his shirt was set loose (or: “the button of his shirt was set loose”), so I inserted my hand in the breast of his shirt and I touched the Seal.”"
"60","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) came out leaning on Usama ibn Zaid"
"61","\When Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) donned a new garment"
"62","\When Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) donned a new garment"
"63","“The apparel dearest to Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) was the hibara [striped garment of Yemenite fabric] that he used to wear.”"
"64","“I saw the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) wearing a red garb, as if I were looking at the sheen of his legs.” Sufyan said: “I think it was a hibara [striped garment of Yemenite fabric].”"
"65","\I never saw anyone among the people more handsome in a red garb than Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace)"
"66","“I saw the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) wearing two green garments.\""
67"""
"67","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Hassan al-Anbari narrated to us, from his two grandmothers, Duhaybah and Ulaybah, from Qaylah bint Makhramah, who said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing two coarse garments dyed with saffron, and he had shaken them off. And in the hadith there is a lengthy story."
"68","Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): “You should acquire white clothes, so that your living ones may wear them, and you can shroud your deceased in them, for they are among the best of your clothes.”"
"69","“Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): 'Wear white, for it is most pure and pleasant, and you must shroud your deceased therein'.”"
"70","'Aisha said;\n“Allah's Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) went out one early morning, wearing a wrap of black hair.”"
"71","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) wore a Byzantine robe with narrow sleeves.”"
